6. Explanation of tables and associations
The topics table stores the list of unique lesson topics like "CSS", "SQL", and others.

Since a lesson can have many topics and a topic can belong to many lessons, we implemented a many-to-many relationship using the join table lesson_topics. 
This table links lessons and topics via their foreign keys lesson_id and topic_id.

7. Description of additional columns and constraints
The topics table includes a unique index on the name column to ensure no duplicate topics exist.

Both tables have timestamps to track creation and update times for data integrity and auditing.

8. Migration details
The create_topics migration defines the topics table with a string column for name and timestamps.

The create_lesson_topics migration defines the join table with lesson_id and topic_id references, foreign key constraints, and timestamps.

